1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
In 1990, Shanghai's Pudong was mostly farmland.
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:05,000
That April, China opened it up — and started building on the fields.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,800
Today Lujiazui is one of the densest skylines on Earth.

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,400
It's topped by the Shanghai Tower — 632 metres, China's tallest.

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,600
Barely thirty years: farmland to a forest of supertalls.

6
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,600
Double-tap if this is the boldest skyline on the planet.

7
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,800
★ Expert Tip: view it from the Bund across the river — the whole wall lines up.

8
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,400
Visionary rebirth, or built too fast to have a soul — which is it?
